    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30745" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nĕpĕta</span></b> , ae,
			f., or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nĕpĕte</span></b> , is,
		n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				city in Etruria</i>, now <i>Nepi</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 5,
				8, § 52</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 6, 21</span></i>; <i><span class="en">10, 14</span></i>; <i><span class="en">27,
			9</span></i>.—Collat. form, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nĕpe</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Vell. 1,
				14, 2</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nĕpĕ-sīnus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nepens-</span></b> ), a,
			um, <i>adj., Nepesine</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ager,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 5,
					19</span></i>
			.—<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nĕpĕsīni</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., <i>the Nepesines</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 6, 9</span></i> and 10.</div>
